The Wounded Warrior Support Foundation continues its active work in support of wounded and injured military servicemen and their families. Donations received in 2026 amounted to GEL 570,387. From January to October, the Foundation allocated GEL 381,414 to 76 wounded and injured warriors, as well as to beneficiaries’ underage children and spouses.
During the reporting period, the Foundation’s assistance comprised:
GEL 149,482 — co-financing jointly with the Ministry of Defense;
GEL 78,004 — support for beneficiaries’ underage children;
GEL 24,851 — support for beneficiaries’ spouses;
GEL 2,887 — adaptation of the living environment.
Silknet founded the Wounded Warrior Support Foundation in 2018 and contributes GEL 300,000 annually to its activities. A range of companies and private individuals donate to the Foundation. Donations are directed toward supporting beneficiaries in healthcare, education, professional re-skilling and social adaptation.
The Foundation is an active supporter of the wounded warrior sports teams of the Ministry of Defense of Georgia and helps improve their training conditions. This year, the Foundation handed over sports wheelchairs to the wheelchair rugby team, equipped the archery team with specialized sports equipment on several occasions, and purchased sports wheelchairs for the wheelchair basketball teams. The wounded warrior sports teams are now preparing for the 2027 Invictus Games in Birmingham, UK.
The Wounded Warrior Support Foundation devotes particular attention to the education and professional re-skilling of wounded warriors and their spouses. The Foundation also regularly finances a range of educational courses for beneficiaries’ underage children.
In September, a dedicated course in computer programming and English was developed for the underage children of veterans. The one-year program started in September and will give several dozen teenagers the opportunity to deepen their knowledge and gain new skills.
The educational programs of the SABADO Leadership Academy are available free of charge to the underage children of the Foundation’s beneficiaries. Last year the Foundation signed a cooperation agreement with the SABADO Leadership Academy, established on the initiative of Davit Bejuashvili’s Education Fund.
